# LSP Fresh-Eyes Audit After Rename + Split Pass — 2026-09-01
# File: openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_09_01_postrename.oot
#
# Method: 8D Red Team applied to the post-rename, post-split LSP state. Negative trust: the rename pass may have left function/file name mismatches.
#
# Result: 1 broken semantic issue (FILE/FUNCTION name mismatch in 5 files, ~30 functions), 1 duplicate function, 3 hand-rolled string helpers. The user was right — the renames did cause issues.
#
# ## 1. e2 Boundary Falsifier: PASS
#
# All 30 distinct import statements across 32 LSP files resolve to real files. 0 broken imports. The rename pass updated the import paths correctly.
#
# ## 2. e3 Data-Path Tracer: FAIL
#
# ### Finding A: FILE/FUNCTION NAME MISMATCH (the user's concern, confirmed)
#
# The previous rename pass renamed 7 files but DID NOT rename the function prefixes inside. This creates a 7-to-30+ mismatch: file name says one thing, function name says another.
#
# The mismatches:
#
# | File | Function prefix | Should be | Mismatch count |
# |---|---|---|---:|
# | lsp_maneuver.oo | lsp_em_* | lsp_maneuver_* | 15+ |
# | lsp_rpc_methods.oo | lsp_methods_* | lsp_rpc_methods_* | 3 |
# | lsp_stdlib_root.oo | lsp_disc_* | lsp_stdlib_root_* | 7 |
# | lsp_compile.oo | lsp_api_* | lsp_compile_* | 3 |
# | lsp_compiler_merge.oo | lsp_compile_* (in merge file) | lsp_compiler_merge_* | 3 |
# | lsp_diagnostics.oo | calls lsp_em_* (in 20+ call sites) | should call lsp_maneuver_* | 20+ |
#
# Concrete examples:
#
# lsp_maneuver.oo defines: lsp_em_cap_text, lsp_em_ps_info, lsp_em_gauge, lsp_em_caps_text, lsp_em_concat_diags, lsp_em_weight_live, lsp_em_ast_weight, lsp_em_d_alloc_live, lsp_em_d_search_live, lsp_em_d_live, lsp_em_eta_live, lsp_em_ps_live, lsp_em_gauge_live, lsp_em_v_default, lsp_em_count_substr
# Should define: lsp_maneuver_cap_text, lsp_maneuver_ps_info, etc.
#
# lsp_rpc_methods.oo defines: lsp_methods_is_lifecycle, lsp_methods_is_document, lsp_methods_is_known
# Should define: lsp_rpc_methods_is_lifecycle, lsp_rpc_methods_is_document, lsp_rpc_methods_is_known
#
# lsp_stdlib_root.oo defines: lsp_disc_env_get, lsp_disc_try_dir, lsp_disc_cwd_candidates, lsp_disc_env_candidates, lsp_disc_binary_locator_candidates, lsp_disc_first_existing, lsp_disc_find_stdlib_root
# Should define: lsp_stdlib_root_env_get, lsp_stdlib_root_try_dir, etc.
#
# lsp_compile.oo defines: lsp_api_match_at, lsp_api_diag_to_severity, lsp_api_walk_fns (and 6 more)
# Should define: lsp_compile_match_at, lsp_compile_diag_to_severity, etc.
#
# lsp_compiler_merge.oo defines: lsp_compile_module_table, lsp_compile_residual_table, lsp_compiler_merge_into_index, lsp_compiler_fetch
# Should define: lsp_compiler_merge_table, lsp_compiler_merge_residual, lsp_compiler_merge_into_index, lsp_compiler_merge_fetch
# (the "compile" prefix in a MERGE file is wrong — the file merges, it doesn't compile)
#
# ### Finding B: DUPLICATE FUNCTION in lsp_server_handlers.oo
#
# `lsp_server_build_index(fs, env, r)` and `lsp_server_refresh_index(fs, env, r)` have IDENTICAL bodies:
#   let rt: String = lsp_disc_find_stdlib_root(fs, env, r);
#   return lsp_scan_stdlib(fs, rt);
# One of them is dead code. Looking at usage: lsp_server_refresh_via_compiler calls lsp_server_refresh_index. So lsp_server_build_index is the dead one (or vice versa).
#
# ## 3. e4 Hermetic Jailor: PASS
#
# Workspace trust guards work. Cap tokens match between callers and callees. URI validation is fail-closed (-32602).
#
# ## 4. e5 Temporal Saboteur: PASS
#
# Double-run proof uses lsp_server_process_message directly. State evolution is immutable (LspServerState is stamped, not mutated).
#
# ## 5. e6 Drag Assassin: PARTIAL
#
# The 4 O(n*m) substring scanners and 6 line counters were deduped in earlier passes. But the fresh-eyes pass found 3 NEW hand-rolled string helpers:
#
# lsp_definition.oo, lsp_hover.oo, lsp_jsonrpc.oo all have hand-rolled starts_with logic:
#   while i < pl { if char_at(s, i) != char_at(prefix, i) { return false; } i = i + 1; }
# Should use: str_starts_with(s, prefix) built-in.
#
# Also: lsp_text.oo has lsp_text_count_lines (correct, 1-line implementation). lsp_diagnostics.oo originally had lsp_em_line_count (was removed in the 8-slice pass). But lsp_completion.oo and lsp_hover.oo have hand-rolled line counters.
#
# ## 6. e7 Semantic Subverter: FAIL (root cause)
#
# The function/file name mismatch IS the semantic subversion. The file name claims to be about "maneuver" but the function names claim to be about "em" (energy-maneuverability). The file name claims to be about "rpc methods" but the function names claim to be about "methods". An IDE developer grepping for "lsp_maneuver" in lsp_maneuver.oo would find nothing, and would find wrong-prefixed functions instead.
#
# ## 7. Verification plan
#
# Fix all the function name mismatches by renaming the function prefixes to match the file names. Update all call sites. The net change should be:
# - lsp_em_* → lsp_maneuver_* (~15 functions in 1 file, ~20 call sites in 4 files)
# - lsp_methods_* → lsp_rpc_methods_* (3 functions in 1 file, ~3 call sites)
# - lsp_disc_* → lsp_stdlib_root_* (7 functions in 1 file, ~3 call sites)
# - lsp_api_* → lsp_compile_* (3+ functions in 1 file, ~5 call sites)
# - lsp_compile_* (in lsp_compiler_merge.oo) → lsp_compiler_merge_* (3 functions, ~3 call sites)
# - Delete 1 duplicate function in lsp_server_handlers.oo
# - Replace 3 hand-rolled starts_with with str_starts_with built-in
#
# Total: ~31 function renames + ~34 call site updates + 1 deletion + 3 helper replacements.
